export const UNDECLARED_BODY_2026_09_19 = [
  "# kanban-comment-and-close",
  "",
  "Comment-and-close on a kanban ticket surface (Linear). The work item asks for one audit comment on a ticket and, once the comment is posted, a state change on that same ticket. Every value that varies per run is an input; nothing here is tied to any one ticket, project, figure or quoted request.",
  "",
  "## When to invoke",
  "",
  "Invoke when a work item asks to record a result on a ticket on a kanban surface and then close that ticket (comment first, then a status change). Preconditions:",
  "",
  "- The target surface is connected (see the Surfaces list). If no connected surface covers the ticket's system, emit no actions and say so in `notes`.",
  "- The candidate carries a ticket identifier and the text or figure the run wants recorded.",
  "- The runbook for the originating surface prescribes the audit read-back (see `## Inputs`).",
  "",
  "## Inputs",
  "",
  "- `<record-id>` — the ticket's identifier on the surface the work came from; read it from the candidate's `Refs:` line or the candidate id. Never invent one.",
  "- `<requested-value>` — the figure or text the candidate or the runbook names for this run (the note body, the recorded exception, the summary). Never a constant in this skill.",
  "- `<reply-channel>` and `<reply-thread>` — from the `Reply target:` line, when the work came from a chat channel or thread. Omitted when the work originated on the ticket surface itself.",
  "- `<originating-surface>` — the slug of the surface the work came from. Its runbook says how the loop is closed there: on a ticket surface, an audit comment then a state change on the ticket; on a chat surface, a reply in the thread.",
  "- `<audit-expectation>` — the read-back the runbook prescribes as evidence (an audit comment visible on the ticket, a returned comment id, a state snapshot).",
  "",
  "## Procedure",
  "",
  "1. Read the candidate. Extract `<record-id>`, `<requested-value>`, the `Reply target:` line (if any) and `<originating-surface>`. Read the runbook for `<originating-surface>` to confirm the comment format, the closing state name and `<audit-expectation>`.",
  "2. Read the ticket before writing. On the `linear` surface, call `get_issue` with `id` set to `<record-id>` to confirm the ticket exists and to learn its current state. Never invent an id, state or result.",
  "3. Compose the comment body from `<requested-value>` in the runbook's format. State the observable work completed and any values deliberately left unknown. Do not add a provenance trailer or a `username`: the server appends the employee name and run id to every comment sent through the shared credential.",
  "4. Emit the audit comment as its own action. On `linear`, this is an `mcp.call` with `tool` `save_comment` and `toolArgsJson` carrying `issueId` and `body` only (a new top-level comment — never send `id` or `parentId`). One action per comment.",
  "5. Emit the state change as its own action, after the comment in the same response. On `linear`, this is an `mcp.call` with `tool` `save_issue` and `toolArgsJson` carrying `id` (the ticket identifier) and `state` set to the workspace's exact closing state name (the argument is `state`, not `status`). Use the closing state only when the requested effect is complete; a partial result gets the comment and the ticket stays in progress. Do not change assignee, priority, labels or description unless the approved action lists it.",
  "6. If the work came from a chat channel or thread (`<reply-channel>` and `<reply-thread>` are present), emit the reply to its source channel and thread as an `http.request` POST to `chat.postMessage` on the connected chat surface, with `channel` set to `<reply-channel>` and `thread_ts` set to `<reply-thread>`. The manager DM never carries a draft reply that belongs in the channel; it may carry a one-line note of what was done.",
  "7. Do not hardcode approval-state language: at execution time read the current mode from the run context and describe effects accordingly (emitted writes land; gated writes wait for the manager's approval of the literal payloads).",
  "",
  "## Actions emitted",
  "",
  "Every run ends with a typed `actions[]` array of work-environment mutations. A run that produces only prose with no actions is broken. Example shapes (values are illustrative):",
  "",
  "```json",
  "[",
  "  {\"tool\": \"mcp.call\", \"args\": {\"surface\": \"linear\", \"tool\": \"save_comment\", \"toolArgsJson\": \"{\\\"issueId\\\":\\\"<record-id>\\\",\\\"body\\\":\\\"<requested-value>\\\"}\"}},",
  "  {\"tool\": \"mcp.call\", \"args\": {\"surface\": \"linear\", \"tool\": \"save_issue\", \"toolArgsJson\": \"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"<record-id>\\\",\\\"state\\\":\\\"<closing-state-name>\\\"}\"}}",
  "]",
  "```",
  "",
  "When a chat reply is owed, append:",
  "",
  "```json",
  "  {\"tool\": \"http.request\", \"args\": {\"surface\": \"slack\", \"method\": \"POST\", \"path\": \"chat.postMessage\", \"headersJson\": \"{\\\"Authorization\\\": \\\"Bearer {{secret}}\\\", \\\"Content-Type\\\": \\\"application/json\\\"}\", \"body\": \"{\\\"channel\\\": \\\"<reply-channel>\\\", \\\"thread_ts\\\": \\\"<reply-thread>\\\", \\\"text\\\": \\\"<reply-text>\\\"}\"}}",
  "```",
  "",
  "Write `{{secret}}` where the credential goes; never include a token value.",
  "",
  "## Verification",
  "",
  "Read back the evidence the runbook prescribes as `<audit-expectation>` before reporting done:",
  "",
  "- On `linear`, re-read the ticket with `get_issue` (`id` = `<record-id>`) and confirm the audit comment is present and the state matches the closing state name sent in step 5.",
  "- If the runbook's `<audit-expectation>` is a returned identifier instead, confirm the comment id returned by `save_comment`.",
  "- If a chat reply was emitted, confirm the post landed in `<reply-channel>` under `<reply-thread>`.",
  "- Report the ticket identifier, the state now on the ticket, and the audit evidence. A partial result is reported as in progress, never as closed.",
].join('\n');

